{"text": " \u542c\u4e0b\u9762\u4e00\u6bb5\u6750\u6599,\u56de\u7b54\u4ee5\u4e0b\u51e0\u4e2a\u5c0f\u9898\u3002 I'm talking to James Sweeney, who's a tree climbing trainer. How did you get interested in trees, James? I grew up around trees because my mother was a garden designer. What really got me into them was that mum had a friend who took care of trees and he offered me a job one summer. And then you went on a course to learn to climb trees. How was that? I was expecting everyone in the class to be young and fit. In fact, there were middle-aged climbers, children, even old people. There was special equipment to make climbing safe. We stayed in the trees for hours because it was so much fun. Then you became a teacher of tree climbing yourself. What do you enjoy most about it? It's great to be in the open, although not so much in the rain or when it's hot. And I like working with people, particularly teaching those who have to go up trees in their work. Most people come because it reminds them of a childhood tree climbing experience. I'm talking to James Sweeney, who's a tree climbing trainer. How did you get interested in trees, James? I grew up around trees because my mother was a garden designer. What really got me into them was that mum had a friend who took care of trees and he offered me a job one summer. And then you went on a course to learn to climb trees. How was that? I was expecting everyone in the class to be young and fit. In fact, there were middle-aged climbers, children, even old people. There was special equipment to make climbing safe. We stayed in the trees for hours because it was so much fun. Then you became a teacher of tree climbing yourself. What do you enjoy most about it? It's great to be in the open, although not so much in the rain or when it's hot. And I like working with people, particularly teaching those who have to go up trees in their work. Most people come because it reminds them of a childhood tree climbing experience.", "segments